  "classification": "subordinate finite residual recovery programme and original Division consumer",
  "claim": "Both fields of the installed CP807 residual drive the finite damped Cayley inverse. The paid exact inverse recovers the old counted pair. The finite recovery error is bounded by q^m times the norm of the actual residual. The original positive-clock Fourier identity and the transported graph defect hold at each finite read. The diagonal limit yields the original resolvent pair, position slots, and independent adjoint K.",
  "scope": "The original calculation authority and current supply a paired lift of the original counted syntax in the old environment and actual adjacent increment. Its typed child is retained in the actual recovery trace, with the original value and effect and the 10+n child charge. The parent pays 10+n+1+m, and its generated relation, inventory, whole and next belong to that recovery calculation. The direct consumer independently reads the paid CP807 update and its original CP321 macro receipt.",
  "negative_controls": "The actual n=0 residual has no exact original R-graph preimage. At m=0 the recovery fields are zero and at m=1 the actual successor field is nonzero.",
